<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 116,914 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 116,914 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 116,914 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 28,900 tonnes on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	  Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			25,106	    17,327</p>
<p>    Import cargo			91,808	    11,573</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, six ships are expected to sail and seven to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Steel		     2,872	Cado Pacific	20/8</p>
<p>Chemical		 10,450	Bakri Orbitor     21/8</p>
<p>Crude oil		65,000	Captain Miranda   21/8</p>
<p>Vegetable oil	  18,600	Kristal	     due</p>
<p>Tallow		    5,500	Juliana	     24/8</p>
<p>Palm oil		 14,400	Ventura	     24/8</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom (9221) 5685192; Fax 5673428</p>
